{\pard\sb360\sa120\keepn\b Reviewer packet \u183? questions-before-priors, round 1\par}
{\pard\sa160 You are asked one question: is what this paper adds of interest to the community this journal serves, under {\f1 interest-criteria.md}?\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab {\f1 paper/} is the paper, written for people; {\f1 appendix/} is the appendix, for the reader who checks.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab {\f1 findings.md} is the machine's findings report from journal run {\f1 20261028-233241-journal-047023d}: form, correspondence and warrant, each finding with a pointer into the record and the standard.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab {\f1 evidence-map.md} places the contribution claim against the corpus. An editor has already signed what is new, on this map.\par}
{\pard\sa160 You are not asked to redo Levels 1 to 3. A review round is a question the author can answer within the existing record: a clarification, a reframed claim, an analysis on materials already there. A request that needs new materials is new work and a new submission.\par}
{\pard\sa160 If you sign that the paper is of interest, your name goes on the certificate. A judgment that it is not produces no public object.\par}
